From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Stedding Authors <noreply@stedding.dev>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 09:49:35 -0400
Subject: add a folder collection type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Arc-style Folders: named, collapsible containers of tabs that nest, hold splits,
and never auto-archive. Introduced as TabCollection::Type::FOLDER, a sibling of
GROUP under UNPINNED, with its own FolderId that is not comparable to
TabGroupId.

Deliberately NOT nested tab groups. Allowing GROUP inside GROUP is a one-line
allow-list change that compiles and then lies: TabModel::UpdateProperties walks
a tab's ancestors and each GROUP overwrites the tab's group id, so the outermost
wins and inner membership disappears from GetGroup(), session restore, saved tab
groups, and every consumer that asks a tab which group it is in. Around
twenty-five further sites assume a group is a contiguous gfx::Range with one id
per tab. None of that is disturbed by a separate type.

Folder membership is intentionally not mirrored onto TabModel for the same
reason: a single optional id would be overwritten by the outermost container.
A tab's folder is read from the collection tree instead.

kFolder is appended to TabStorageType rather than inserted, because those values
are persisted.

FolderView is a plain vertical container for now. The header row, collapse
affordance and drop target arrive with the sidebar work; a folder that renders
as a bare container is obviously unfinished, which is better than one that looks
finished and behaves wrongly.

Why: Folders are required for 1.0 and were the highest Arc-named request on the
comparable project — users said they would not leave Arc without collapsible
pinned folders.
Removable when: upstream ships an equivalent nestable, non-archiving tab
container that Folders can be rebased onto.
